{
    "type": "game",
    "name": "Fever Meme",
    "steam_appid": 3110070,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fever Meme is a comedy/parody game that pivots between multiple genres as it spits in the face of traditional game design. <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3110070/extras/76573acb5015a1554b89c2a4e5af0434.poster.avif?t=1753215645\" width=616 height=240 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3110070/extras/76573acb5015a1554b89c2a4e5af0434.webm?t=1753215645\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3110070/extras/76573acb5015a1554b89c2a4e5af0434.mp4?t=1753215645\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span>One moment you'll be in a 2007-esque rage platformer, the next moment you'll be in the game show with a giant spider. But beneath all of the trolls and humor is a deeper overarching story. The game is self-aware of your actions as you play, your past mistakes, and so much more. And the further you make it into the game, the more the dynamic between player and creator is explored as the fourth wall is completely stripped away.<br><br><strong>DISCLAIMER: Do not play if you are prone to photosensitive epilepsy or are sensitive to loud audio.</strong></p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fever Meme is a comedy/parody game that pivots between multiple genres as it spits in the face of traditional game design. <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3110070/extras/76573acb5015a1554b89c2a4e5af0434.poster.avif?t=1753215645\" width=616 height=240 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3110070/extras/76573acb5015a1554b89c2a4e5af0434.webm?t=1753215645\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3110070/extras/76573acb5015a1554b89c2a4e5af0434.mp4?t=1753215645\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span>One moment you'll be in a 2007-esque rage platformer, the next moment you'll be in the game show with a giant spider. But beneath all of the trolls and humor is a deeper overarching story. The game is self-aware of your actions as you play, your past mistakes, and so much more. And the further you make it into the game, the more the dynamic between player and creator is explored as the fourth wall is completely stripped away.<br><br><strong>DISCLAIMER: Do not play if you are prone to photosensitive epilepsy or are sensitive to loud audio.</strong></p>",
    "short_description": "This game is a cross between The Stanley Parable, Undertale, and rage games like I Wanna Be the Guy. And the deeper you get, the less the fourth wall is respected. This game is a parody of game design and laughs on the surface, but there is a deeper and darker story to this game's origin to unravel.",
    "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support",
    "reviews": "\u201cFever Meme is an incredibly overstimulating game. It\u2019s brash, bold, and incredibly in-your-face at almost every moment.\u201d<br>Highly Recommended \u2013 VICE<br><br>\u201cBut, like The Stanley Parable, it\u2019s a case where you have to see it to understand it.\u201d<br>7.5/10 \u2013 <br><br>\u201cIf you enjoy satire and games where choices truly matter, this one may surprise you.\u201d<br>4.2/5 \u2013 Softonic<br>",
